/** @mainpage Qore Ssh Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section sshintro Ssh Module Introduction

    The Ssh module provides server-side SSH and SFTP support for Qore through
    <a href="https://www.libssh.org/">libssh</a>. The module is designed for controlled command processing, auditable
    file transfer, and integration scenarios.

    The current API shape and design direction are documented in the source
    tree in <tt>design/api-spec.md</tt>.

    Features include:
    - typed server-side SSH and SFTP contracts in
      @ref Qore::Ssh "Qore::Ssh"
    - live SSH command and SFTP server flows through
      @ref Qore::Ssh::SshServer "SshServer"
    - helper/service logger support through @c Qore::Logger::LoggerInterface
    - strongly typed virtual SFTP helper, backend, and provider APIs
    - full SFTP protocol support including symlink, readlink, setstat, and the
      @c statvfs\@openssh.com extension
    - configurable cipher, KEX, MAC, and host-key algorithm restrictions
    - per-listener IP allow/deny filtering with CIDR support
    - server-side keepalive probes and idle session timeouts
    - RFC 4252 pre-authentication banner support
    - multi-factor / partial authentication with configurable required methods
    - active session enumeration through
      @ref Qore::Ssh::SshServer::listActiveSessions() "SshServer::listActiveSessions()"
    - SFTP read-ahead pipelining through
      @ref Qore::Ssh::SftpSession::processRequests() "SftpSession::processRequests()"
    - generic local-server @c ConnectionProvider infrastructure with grouped
      security options
    - generic SFTP exchange @c DataProvider infrastructure with inbound events
    - virtual filesystem persistence with snapshot and write-through modes
    - repository-standard directory-module layout for all qlib user modules

    The intended public binary-module namespace is:
    - @ref Qore::Ssh "Qore::Ssh"

    The initial public classes include:
    - @ref Qore::Ssh::SshServer "Qore::Ssh::SshServer"

    Generic user modules in this repository include:
    - @ref sshserverconnectionsintro "SshServerConnections"
      - provides
        @ref SshServerConnections::AbstractSshServerConnection,
        @ref SshServerConnections::SshCommandServerConnection, and
        @ref SshServerConnections::SftpServerConnection
      - registers the local server connection schemes
        @c sshsrv, @c sshserver, @c sftpsrv, and @c sftpserver
      - returns live @ref Qore::Ssh::SshServer "Qore::Ssh::SshServer"
        objects from the @c ConnectionProvider API and projects typed
        @ref Qore::Ssh::SshServerConfig "Qore::Ssh::SshServerConfig" /
        @ref Qore::Ssh::SshListenerConfig "Qore::Ssh::SshListenerConfig"
        hashes through
        @c getServerConfig() and @c getListenerConfig()
      - supports grouped listener-side operational caps through
        @ref sshserverconnections-sshserverconnectionlimits "SshServerConnectionLimits", including
        @c max_sessions
      - supports grouped listener service controls through
        @ref sshserverconnections-sshserverconnectionservices "SshServerConnectionServices", including @c enabled_auth_methods,
        @c allow_command_service, and @c allow_sftp_service
      - supports grouped typed authentication through
        @ref sshserverauthproviderintro "SshServerAuthProvider" or explicit
        @c auth_provider objects
    - @ref sshserverauthproviderintro "SshServerAuthProvider"
      - provides
        @ref SshServerAuthProvider::AbstractSshAuthProvider and
        @ref SshServerAuthProvider::VirtualSshAuthProvider
      - supports config-driven and custom object-driven authentication for
        @c none, @c password, @c publickey, @c interactive, @c hostbased,
        and @c gssapi-mic
    - @ref sshservercommandproviderintro "SshServerCommandProvider"
      - provides
        @ref SshServerCommandProvider::VirtualSshCommandService
        for generic command virtualization through
        @ref SshServerConnections::SshCommandServerConnection
      - intentionally does not add a command-side @c DataProvider layer
    - @ref sftpserverdataproviderintro "SftpServerDataProvider"
      - includes a config-driven observable event action
        @c inbound-file-accepted for inbound uploads
      - the observable event contract includes typed
        @c inbound-file-accepted and @c inbound-file-rejected events
      - exposes typed outbound completion events
        @c outbound-file-claimed, @c outbound-file-archived, and
        @c outbound-file-deleted
      - exposes a typed inbound acceptance policy for helper, provider, and
        live-upload enforcement, including principal-aware acceptance and
        routing plus duplicate-name, duplicate-size, duplicate-content,
        file-count, and total-byte rejection

    The qlib convenience layer includes:
    - @ref sshserverconnections-sshserverconnectionlimits "SshServerConnectionLimits" for grouped
      listener operational caps such as @c max_sessions
    - @ref SshServerAuthProvider::VirtualSshAuthProvider for config-driven
      and custom object-driven authentication
      - accepts an optional @c LoggerInterface and logs auth attempts at
        @c detail, accepted auth at @c info, and rejected auth at @c warn
    - logger-aware helper/service objects that accept @c LoggerInterface:
      @ref SshServerConnections::AbstractSshServerConnection,
      @ref SshServerCommandProvider::VirtualSshCommandService,
      @ref SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpFilesystem, and
      @ref SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpExchange
      - command virtualization logs accepted requests at @c info, rejected
        requests at @c warn, and configuration changes at @c debug
      - virtual filesystem churn logs at @c detail and event-listener callback
        failures log at @c error
    - @ref SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpFilesystem for easy in-memory
      virtual SFTP filesystems and atomic submit/retrieve workflows
      - includes inspection helpers such as @c listFilePaths(),
        @c listDirectoryPaths(), and @c exportSnapshot()
    - @ref SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpExchange for explicit inbound and
      outbound exchange-style SFTP backends
    - @ref SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpExchangeRecordStore for
      record-oriented queue-style exchange APIs
    - strongly typed helper hashes for constructor options and requests:
      @ref sftpserverdataprovider-virtualsftpfilesystemoptions "SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpFilesystemOptions",
      @ref sftpserverdataprovider-virtualsftpexchangeoptions "SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpExchangeOptions",
      @ref sftpserverdataprovider-virtualsftppathrequest "SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpPathRequest",
      @ref sftpserverdataprovider-virtualsftpsubmissionrequest "SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpSubmissionRequest", and
      @ref sftpserverdataprovider-virtualsftpcompletionrequest "SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpCompletionRequest"
    - strongly typed record-store request hashes:
      @ref sftpserverdataprovider-virtualsftprecordrequest "SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpRecordRequest",
      @ref sftpserverdataprovider-virtualsftprecordsubmissionrequest "SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpRecordSubmissionRequest", and
      @ref sftpserverdataprovider-virtualsftprecordcompletionrequest "SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpRecordCompletionRequest"
    - strongly typed inbound policy hash:
      @ref sftpserverdataprovider-virtualsftpinboundpolicy "SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpInboundPolicy"
    - strongly typed helper hashes for snapshots, listings, and records:
      @ref sftpserverdataprovider-virtualsftpfilesnapshot "SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpFileSnapshot",
      @ref sftpserverdataprovider-virtualsftpsnapshot "SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpSnapshot",
      @ref sftpserverdataprovider-virtualsftpentryinfo "SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpEntryInfo", and
      @ref sftpserverdataprovider-virtualsftprecordinfo "SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpRecordInfo"
    - built-in helper-managed state is projected separately through
      @ref sftpserverdataprovider-virtualsftpbuiltinstate "SftpServerDataProvider::VirtualSftpBuiltinState", so stable flags such
      as archived, claimed, and exchange role do not need to be read from
      loose metadata
      - for delete-style completion results, @c VirtualSftpRecordInfo.path may
        be @c NOTHING because no final path remains
    - runnable examples in @c examples/VirtualSftpFilesystem.qtest and
      @c examples/VirtualSftpExchangeRecordStore.qtest
    - a low-level real server example in @c examples/VirtualSftpServer.qr
    - a real policy-and-event server example in
      @c examples/VirtualSftpInboundPolicyServer.qr

    Recommended helper usage is to prefer the typed request hashes over loose
    request maps for both exchange and record-store operations. The virtual
    filesystem and exchange backends also expose typed overloads for the
    backend verbs using @ref Qore::Ssh "Qore::Ssh" typed hashes such as
    @ref Qore::Ssh::SftpPathRequest "SftpPathRequest",
    @ref Qore::Ssh::SftpOpenRequest "SftpOpenRequest",
    @ref Qore::Ssh::SftpRenameRequest "SftpRenameRequest",
    @ref Qore::Ssh::SftpReadRequest "SftpReadRequest",
    @ref Qore::Ssh::SftpReadResult "SftpReadResult",
    @ref Qore::Ssh::SftpWriteRequest "SftpWriteRequest",
    @ref Qore::Ssh::SftpCloseRequest "SftpCloseRequest",
    @ref Qore::Ssh::SftpPathInfo "SftpPathInfo",
    @ref Qore::Ssh::SftpListResult "SftpListResult",
    @ref Qore::Ssh::SftpOpenResult "SftpOpenResult", and
    @ref Qore::Ssh::SftpOperationResult "SftpOperationResult". The remaining loose backend
    maps remain available for dynamic backends; @ref Qore::Ssh::SftpSession "SftpSession" dispatches typed backend
    request hashes directly for both low-level filesystem verbs and streamed
    handle verbs.
    The higher-level @ref Qore::Ssh::SftpSession "SftpSession" convenience helpers support typed
    request overloads, so callers can stay inside the typed API for
    submit/retrieve/complete flows instead of dropping back to primitive
    arguments plus loose metadata.
    Retrieval completion uses an explicit typed
    @c completion_mode field on
    @ref Qore::Ssh::SftpOperationRequest "SftpOperationRequest".
    Inbound acceptance can be configured through a typed
    @ref sftpserverdataprovider-virtualsftpinboundpolicy "VirtualSftpInboundPolicy"
    with filename glob/regex controls, size
    bounds, overwrite control, and hidden-file policy.

    The command-side typed contract is intentionally smaller:
    - @ref Qore::Ssh::SshCommandRequest "SshCommandRequest" carries stable session
      identity plus routing data such as @c command, @c arguments, and
      @c metadata.request_type
    - @ref Qore::Ssh::SshCommandResult "SshCommandResult" carries stable
      @c accepted, @c exit_status, @c stdout, @c stderr, and @c result_data
      fields
    - command virtualization is intentionally connection-backed and does not
      add a command-side @c DataProvider abstraction

    The generic infrastructure in this repository is split deliberately:
    - generic @c ConnectionProvider infrastructure for both command and SFTP
      server virtualization
    - generic @c DataProvider infrastructure only for the SFTP/file-exchange
      side
    - no command-side @c DataProvider abstraction
    This includes a
    @ref sftpserverdataproviderintro "SftpServerDataProvider"
    factory/app/provider layer on top of the typed virtual exchange helpers,
    including a config-driven inbound file submission event action for local
    SFTP servers. The focused design note for that work is in
    <tt>design/data-provider-infrastructure.md</tt>.

